Implemented Story 2.1 and updated the story artifact to `ready-for-review` in [2-1-keep-the-departure-picture-current-during-normal-operation.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/2-1-keep-the-departure-picture-current-during-normal-operation.md).

The public route now server-renders from the new dashboard service and same-origin API in [page.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/app/(public)/page.tsx) and [route.ts](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/app/api/dashboard/route.ts). I added canonical API/contract handling, snapshot build/publish/persist flow under [dashboard-service.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/server/dashboard/dashboard-service.js), [build-dashboard-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/server/dashboard/build-dashboard-snapshot.js), and [snapshot-store.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/server/cache/snapshot-store.js), plus TfL and WeatherAPI adapters with Zod validation. The UI keeps the existing shell but now polls through [DashboardLiveScreen.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/DashboardLiveScreen.tsx) and [useDashboardQuery.ts](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/hooks/useDashboardQuery.ts), with calm currentness wording updated in [AtmosphericHeader.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/AtmosphericHeader.tsx).

Validation passed: `npm run validate`. I also added live-path coverage in [dashboard.live-path.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.live-path.test.mjs) and extended [startup-smoke.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/smoke/startup-smoke.test.mjs). One implementation note: because the workspace could not install `@tanstack/react-query`, I preserved the planned import surface with a local compatibility shim at [tanstack-react-query.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/vendor/tanstack-react-query.tsx). Live provider reads use the normal path when `TFL_*` and `WEATHERAPI_*` env vars are available; otherwise the service serves the last safe or fixture-backed snapshot through the same orchestration path.
