Findings from the review, all auto-fixed:

- High: fallback snapshots could surface a fabricated `steady` trend with no 15-minute evidence, violating AC1. Fixed in [overall-departure-snapshot.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/data/overall-departure-snapshot.js#L6) and [dashboard-service.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/server/dashboard/dashboard-service.js#L23).
- Medium: the presenter still emitted a trend-style message when `overallTrend` was `null`, which created a false cue even when no approved trend existed. Fixed in [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js#L32) and [AtmosphericHeader.tsx](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/components/AtmosphericHeader.tsx#L1).
- Medium: reduced-confidence copy used contract-like jargon, and fixture fallback trust stayed too optimistic after live rebuild failure. Fixed in [freshness.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/contracts/freshness.js#L28) and [dashboard-service.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/lib/server/dashboard/dashboard-service.js#L23).

