codex
Findings fixed during review:

- Coverage gap: Story 2.3 claimed backward-safe disruption defaults, but there was no regression test proving older snapshots normalize correctly. Fixed in [tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs).
- Coverage gap: Story 2.3 required disruption to come only from approved service-state triggers, but there was no test proving stale/degraded confidence alone does not create serious disruption. Fixed in [tests/unit/dashboard.live-path.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.live-path.test.mjs).
- Review artifact gap: the story lacked a senior review record and sprint tracking still showed `review`. Fixed in [2-3-surface-serious-disruption-without-breaking-composure.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/2-3-surface-serious-disruption-without-breaking-composure.md) and [sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml).

The implementation itself validated cleanly after the review fixes. I marked the story `done`, appended a `Senior Developer Review (AI)` section, and synced sprint status to `done`.

Verification passed with `npm run validate`.
